From: MyNaai Dev <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] App: both subscription screens read the plan list from the backend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The app carried two price lists, and they had drifted: registration sold
₹199/₹299/₹499 with a free card reading "20 days", while the renewal screen still
showed the old ₹99/₹179/₹249 ladder. A partner was quoted one price and charged
another on the very next screen.

  · `src/services/planCatalog.js` — fetch, normalize, cache, and a
    `usePlanCatalog()` hook. The seed renders on the first frame and the backend's
    rows replace it, so a slow network never leaves a partner on a spinner at the
    moment they are about to pay. Reads `mynaai:plan-catalog:v2` from AsyncStorage
    when the endpoint is unreachable; only a real remote answer overwrites it.
  · `communication.listPartnerPlans()` — `POST /api/salons/plans/list`, no token.
  · Both subscription screens drop their local arrays: cards, ribbon (the row's
    own `badge`), price label and duration all come from the catalog, and the free
    card's duration is the backend's trial length instead of `20 days`.
  · Durations are re-derived from the day count, so a row edited to 100 days reads
    "100 Days". The pay action sends the numeric price — the backend refuses a
    mismatch with its stored price, so an app that has not refreshed fails loudly
    instead of paying an old price.
  · A plan taken off sale disappears from the list; an already-gone selection
    says "This plan is no longer on sale" instead of crashing on `undefined.price`.

Verified: every touched file parses; `describeDuration` at 1/30/60/90/100/365/0
days and `formatPrice` at 0/199/1299.5; the normalizer against a real response
shape, a legacy `planList` shape and `null`; `loadPlanCatalog` online (cache
written), offline with a cache (previous rows, not the seed) and offline cold
(seed).
